msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:89
msgid "Everybody who bought a ticket is refunded in full, booking fee included, to the card that paid. You do not need to ask — the money goes back automatically within five working days and we write to tell you it has."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:140
msgid "Event Ticket Booking"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:145
msgid "Event Ticket Booking FAQ"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:176
#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:181
#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:186
#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:659
#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:664
msgid "Booking"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:177
msgid "How do I book a home service?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:178
msgid "Pick the service you need, choose a time that suits you, add your address and confirm. The booking is accepted straight away and matched to a verified professional working in your area — there is no callback to wait for."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:182
msgid "What happens after booking confirmation?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:183
msgid "You get a confirmation with the name and photograph of the professional assigned to you, and a message on the morning of the visit with a narrower arrival window. Both also appear under Bookings in your account."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:187
msgid "Can I reschedule my booking easily?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:188
msgid "Up to four hours before the slot, yes, and as many times as you need. Open the booking, choose a new slot, and the professional is notified for you. Inside four hours it counts as a late change and a small fee applies."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:191
#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:201
msgid "Service"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:192
msgid "How are service professionals assigned?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:193
msgid "By trade, by distance and by rating, in that order. Everybody on the platform is background checked and carries their own insurance, and anyone whose rating falls below four stars stops receiving new work until it recovers."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:196
#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:380
#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:385
msgid "Payment"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:197
msgid "What payment methods are available?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:198
msgid "Card, bank transfer and the usual digital wallets. Nothing is taken until the job is marked complete, so a visit that does not happen is never a visit you have paid for."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:202
msgid "How is service quality ensured?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:203
msgid "Every job is rated, and every rating is read. Work that falls short is put right at our expense within seven days — you do not pay twice to have something finished properly."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:269
msgid "Home Service Booking"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:274
msgid "Easy Home Service Booking Guide"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:300
msgid "Consulting"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:301
msgid "How can business consulting improve company growth?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:302
msgid "Consulting helps an organisation see where the opportunities actually are, work through the operational problems holding it back, and put a plan behind the answer. The value is rarely the advice on its own — it is having someone whose whole job that week is the decision you have been putting off."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:306
msgid "Why is professional IT support important?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:307
msgid "Because the cost of an outage is almost never the outage. Monitored systems, tested backups and somebody who answers out of hours turn a day lost into an hour lost, and that difference compounds across a year."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:310
msgid "Marketing"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:311
msgid "What benefits does digital marketing provide?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:312
msgid "Reach you can measure and spend you can stop. Every channel reports what it returned, which means the budget moves towards what is working rather than towards what was agreed in January."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:315
msgid "Delivery"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:316
msgid "How does project management ensure success?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:317
msgid "By making scope, owner and date visible to everyone at once. Most projects do not fail on capability — they fail because two people held different versions of the same deadline for six weeks."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:321
msgid "Why invest in customer support services?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:322
msgid "Support is where a customer finds out whether the promise was real. It is also the cheapest research a company can buy: the same three questions arriving every week are a product decision waiting to be made."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:372
msgid "FAQs"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:374
msgid "Frequently Asked Questions About Business Services"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:387
msgid "Business Services"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:427
#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:433
msgid "Styles"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:428
msgid "What makes bold abstract art so visually powerful?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:429
msgid "Abstract work gives up the job of depicting something, and gets colour, form and texture back in exchange. Nothing in the frame tells you what to think about it, so the reading is yours — which is why two people can stand in front of the same canvas and describe two different paintings."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:434
msgid "How does minimalist line art say so much with so little?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:435
msgid "By trusting the eye to finish the sentence. A single continuous line describing a shoulder reads as a whole figure because we supply the rest without noticing, and the restraint is what makes the gesture land."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:439
#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:445
msgid "Medium"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:440
msgid "Can digital tools replace canvas and paintbrush?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:441
msgid "They replace some of the constraints, not the practice. Undo, layers and infinite colour change what is easy, but they do not change what is worth making — and plenty of painters work in both without feeling they have swapped one for the other."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:446
msgid "Why is mixed media considered the most expressive form?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:447
msgid "Because the materials argue with each other. Paper against paint against thread gives a surface with real depth and real accident in it, and the places where two materials refuse to sit together are usually the places the eye goes first."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:504
msgid "Gallery Questions"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:509
msgid "About the Work"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:510
msgid "What people ask most often about the pieces on show."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:541
#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:546
#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:650
#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:655
msgid "Products"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:542
#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:651
msgid "What materials do you use?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:543
msgid "Solid North American oak, top-grain leather and recycled fabric, and nothing that needs an asterisk. Every piece is built the way furniture was built before veneer became the default, which is the reason we are comfortable quoting decades rather than years."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:547
#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:656
msgid "Is assembly required for items?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:548
msgid "Most pieces arrive assembled. The few that do not — beds, and the larger dining tables — take two people about twenty minutes with the tool included in the box, and there is nothing to buy separately."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:551
#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:556
#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:561
#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:660
#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:665
#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:670
#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:383
#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:388
msgid "Orders"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:552
#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:661
msgid "Do you offer custom sizes?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:553
msgid "On tables, shelving and beds, yes. Send the measurements you need and you will have a quote and a lead time within two working days. Custom pieces carry the same guarantee as everything else."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:557
#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:666
msgid "What is your shipping cost?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:558
msgid "Free above the order threshold, a flat rate below it, and no surcharge for a piece being heavy or awkward. Delivery is to the room of your choice, not to the kerb."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:562
#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:671
msgid "Can I order fabric samples?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:563
msgid "Up to five swatches, posted free. Colour on a screen is a promise nobody can keep, so we would much rather you held the fabric next to your floor before deciding."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:614
msgid "Materials & Care"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:619
msgid "Before You Order"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:652
msgid "Solid oak, top-grain leather and recycled fabric throughout. The specification for every piece is published on its own page, down to the finish and the hardware, because a material list nobody can check is just a adjective."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:657
msgid "Rarely. Most pieces arrive built; the few that do not come with the tool and a single sheet of instructions, and take two people about twenty minutes."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:662
msgid "On tables, shelving and beds. Send your measurements and a quote comes back within two working days, with the same guarantee as a stock piece."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:667
msgid "Free above the order threshold and a flat rate below it, delivered to the room you want it in rather than left at the door."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:672
msgid "Five swatches, posted free, no order required. Screens lie about colour and we would rather you found that out before the sofa arrives."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:723
msgid "If your question is not listed here, reach out and we will help."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:724
#: includes/Templates/ShowcaseSet.php:643
msgid "Contact Us"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:729
msgid "Your Questions, Answered"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DesignSet.php:743
msgid "Questions Answered"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:54
msgid "How do I know if it is you or me?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:55
msgid "Check the status page first — it is hosted separately, so it stays up when we do not. If everything there is green, it is worth trying a different network before writing to us."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:59
msgid "What counts as an incident?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:60
msgid "Anything that stops you doing something you could do an hour ago. Slower than usual counts as degraded, and we post those too rather than hoping nobody notices."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:67
msgid "Can I be told automatically?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:68
msgid "Subscribe on the status page for email or a webhook. Both fire within a minute of an incident opening and again when it closes."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:72
msgid "Do you publish post-mortems?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:73
msgid "For anything over fifteen minutes, within five working days, with what broke and what changed so it does not again. Names are left out; causes are not."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:80
msgid "Do you have downtime windows?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:81
msgid "Planned work is announced a week ahead and scheduled between 02:00 and 04:00 UTC on a Sunday. Most releases need no window at all."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:87
msgid "Real-Time Status"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:88
msgid "Current system state and incident classification."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:94
msgid "Notifications & Reports"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:95
msgid "Automated alerts, webhooks, and post-mortem logs."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:100
msgid "Scheduled Maintenance"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:101
msgid "Planned downtime windows and maintenance schedules."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:107
msgid "Status & Incidents"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:112
msgid "Status and incidents"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:113
msgid "What we post, when we post it, and how to be told without checking."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:149
msgid "Ask AI Assistant"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:154
msgid "Get in touch"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:155
msgid "Try the quick way first. Most questions are already answered somewhere on this site."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:159
msgid "Ask first"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:160
msgid "Most questions are already answered somewhere on this site."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:166
#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:767
msgid "Still need help? Write to us."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:171
#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:369
msgid "How do I reset my password?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:172
msgid "Where is my invoice?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:173
msgid "How do I move my licence?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:194
msgid "Keyboard"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:195
msgid "Can everything be used without a mouse?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:196
msgid "Yes. Every question is a real button, focus is always visible, and nothing traps the keyboard inside it. Tab and Enter reach everything a click does."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:199
#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:204
msgid "Screen readers"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:200
msgid "Is open and closed announced?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:201
msgid "Each question carries its expanded state and points at the answer it controls, so a screen reader says whether it is open before you decide to open it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:205
msgid "Which readers do you test with?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:206
msgid "NVDA on Windows and VoiceOver on macOS and iOS. Those three cover most of the people who write to us about it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:209
msgid "Motion"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:210
msgid "Can I turn the animation off?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:211
msgid "It turns itself off. If your system asks for reduced motion, panels open instantly instead of sliding, and nothing moves under the pointer."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:214
#: build/blocks/faq-form/index.js:272
#: build/blocks/faq-form/index.js:273
#: build/blocks/image-faq/index.js:413
#: build/blocks/image-faq/index.js:414
msgid "Colour"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:215
msgid "Do the default colours pass contrast?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:216
msgid "Every default combination meets AA for body text. Once you change them that is yours to check, and the contrast figure is shown beside the colour picker."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:219
msgid "Reporting"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:220
msgid "I found a barrier. Who do I tell?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:221
msgid "Write to us with the page and what happened. Accessibility reports are treated as bugs rather than requests, and they go to the front of the queue."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:226
#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:231
msgid "Accessibility"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:232
msgid "What works, what we test, and where to tell us it does not."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:252
msgid "Do I have to remove the old plugin first?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:253
msgid "No, and you should not. Leave it active until the new pages are published, then deactivate rather than delete for a fortnight."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:257
msgid "Will my URLs change?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:258
msgid "Not unless you move the pages. FAQs live inside a page here rather than having addresses of their own."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:265
msgid "Can I bring the questions across automatically?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:266
msgid "From the common formats, yes. From a page builder's own accordion, usually not — those store content in a shape only they can read."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:270
msgid "What about my styling?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:271
msgid "It does not come with them, and that is a feature. Pick the closest theme and adjust; matching the old plugin exactly usually means keeping choices you had stopped liking."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:275
msgid "What if the two clash on one page?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:276
msgid "Switch schema off on one of them. Two sets of FAQ markup is the only real conflict, and it is a setting rather than a code change."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:283
msgid "Will search rankings drop?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:284
msgid "Not from this, as long as the questions and answers stay on the same URLs and stay visible without clicking. Keep the wording and you keep the position."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:288
msgid "How long should I keep the old one?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:289
msgid "Two weeks, deactivated. Long enough to spot a page you forgot, short enough that nobody reactivates it by accident."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:295
msgid "Before you start"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:296
msgid "Two things worth knowing, both of which save an afternoon."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:302
msgid "Moving the content"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:303
msgid "What comes across on its own and what has to be retyped."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:308
#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:71
#: includes/Templates/ShowcaseSet.php:748
msgid "Afterwards"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:309
msgid "Rankings, and when it is safe to delete the old plugin."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:314
msgid "Want us to check it?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:315
msgid "Send the URL of one migrated page before you do the rest. We would rather look at one than untangle thirty."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:320
msgid "Migration Guide"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:325
msgid "Moving from another plugin"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:326
msgid "Three stages, and the honest answer on what does not come across."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:365
#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:370
#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:375
msgid "Paperwork"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:366
msgid "Can you complete our vendor questionnaire?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:367
msgid "Yes, and usually within three working days. Send it early — it is the step that delays these the most, and it is rarely the buyer who is slow."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:371
msgid "Will you sign our contract instead of yours?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:372
msgid "We will read it and mark what we cannot agree to, which is usually two clauses about unlimited liability. Everything else is negotiable."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:376
msgid "Do you have a DPA?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:377
msgid "One that is pre-signed and downloadable, with sub-processors listed. If your legal team wants changes, send them and we will look."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:381
msgid "Can we pay by invoice and purchase order?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:382
msgid "Annually, by bank transfer, on thirty-day terms. Quarterly is possible above a threshold; monthly invoicing is not."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:386
msgid "Is there a discount for multi-year?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:387
msgid "Two years at ten per cent, three at fifteen, and the rate is locked for the term. Ask rather than assuming it is on the pricing page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:391
msgid "What we can send today"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:394
msgid "Pre-signed data processing agreement"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:395
msgid "Sub-processor list and hosting locations"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:396
msgid "Insurance certificate and company details"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:397
msgid "Accessibility conformance statement"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:398
msgid "A quote against a purchase order"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:401
msgid "Ask for all five in one email and they come back in one reply."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:402
msgid "Request the pack"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:405
msgid "Enterprise & Procurement"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:410
msgid "For procurement"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:437
#: includes/Templates/ShowcaseSet.php:807
msgid "Does it work with my page builder?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:438
msgid "Through a shortcode anywhere a builder gives you a text field, and as a native block in the block editor. Both produce the same markup."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:444
msgid "Will my SEO plugin conflict?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:445
msgid "Only over FAQ schema, and only if both are printing it. Switch it off in one of the two and they stay out of each other's way."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:450
#: includes/Templates/ShowcaseSet.php:825
msgid "Is it translation ready?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:451
msgid "Every string goes through the translation functions, and the multilingual plugins treat each FAQ as translatable content."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:456
msgid "What about caching and optimisation?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:457
msgid "Nothing here needs to be excluded from a cache. Styles and scripts load per block and only on pages using one, so combining them is safe."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:462
msgid "Is there a hook for developers?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:463
msgid "Filters on the query, the output and the schema, and a REST route for the library. All documented rather than discovered."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:469
msgid "Integrations"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:474
msgid "What it works with"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:475
msgid "The compatibility questions, answered without a matrix nobody reads."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:506
msgid "Where do the questions live?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:507
msgid "In your own WordPress database, as ordinary posts. Nothing about your library is stored anywhere else, and there is no account to create."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:511
msgid "What about form submissions?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:512
msgid "Also your database. They hold the name and email the visitor typed, which is why deleting one is permanent and says so before it happens."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:516
msgid "And the AI answers?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:517
msgid "The question and the matching FAQ text are sent to the model to compose a reply. No visitor identity goes with it, and nothing is used for training."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:524
msgid "Who can see submissions?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:525
msgid "Anyone who can edit pages on your site, and nobody else. It follows your existing roles rather than adding permissions of its own."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:529
msgid "Can I export or delete on request?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:530
msgid "Both, from the Form Submissions screen, and a delete is a real delete rather than a flag. That is what makes a subject access request answerable in minutes."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:537
msgid "How do you handle vulnerability reports?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:538
msgid "Acknowledged within one working day, fixed and released before it is described publicly, and the reporter credited if they want to be."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:542
msgid "Is the code audited?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:543
msgid "Every release goes through automated checks, and every input is validated before it reaches a database or a stylesheet. Independent review has happened twice."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:549
msgid "Where your data lives"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:550
msgid "Three different answers, depending on which data you mean."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:556
msgid "Who can reach it"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:557
msgid "Roles, exports, and deleting on request."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:562
#: includes/Templates/ShowcaseSet.php:760
msgid "How we work"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:563
msgid "Reports, releases and review."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:568
msgid "Reporting something"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:569
msgid "Use the security address rather than the support form, so it reaches somebody who can act on it the same day."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:574
msgid "Security & Privacy"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:579
msgid "Security and privacy"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/DetailSet.php:580
msgid "Where things are kept, who can reach them, and what happens when somebody finds a hole."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:56
#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:61
#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:66
