#: build/ask-ai-promo/index.js:61
msgid "The model never sees your database, your pages or the open web. It receives the visitor's question plus the entries that matched it — your FAQs and your own written answers, nothing else — and is instructed to answer from those alone. When nothing matches closely enough, the visitor is shown related questions rather than a confident guess, and you get told about it on the Asked Questions page."
msgstr ""

#: build/ask-ai-promo/index.js:63
msgid "Visitors are counted by a one-way hash of their address, never by the address itself, and only question text is stored — no names, no addresses, no session data. The AI provider only ever receives the question and the entries of your own that matched it."
